Z||000000||Rodney||08-05-2001||09:46 AM||||I'm looking to reproduce the Mera/308 kit car tail pipes<BR>soon. The originals were mild steel and painted black.<BR>They do rust away in time. I am considering 304<BR>stainless steel but then they are always a silvery<BR>finish and paint will not stick to them well. Looking<BR>for Mera/308 kit owners opinions on what material to<BR>use.<P>Thanks,<BR>Rodney Dickman<BR>New web page! <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rodneydickman.com</A> <P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||08-05-2001||09:51 AM||||what is the routing going to be on your setup. Id like to run new pipes from my mufflers thru the exits in rear panel. Id like to have stainless myself. Id prefer black color......maybe powder coating?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rodney||08-05-2001||11:14 AM||||The original routing is around the lower sides of the trunk and then a sharp turn thru the openings in the rear lower valance. The original Meras had a cut in the body to allow the pipes to go around the trunk on the underside along the sides of the lower trunk area. If the kit builder copied a Mera as it was originally then your car should have these open areas.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||08-05-2001||06:52 PM||||keep me posted. show some pics when your thru. or email me. thanks||||reg||1
Z||000004||308||08-05-2001||11:11 PM||||Rodney, Just instaled all the new stuff I got from you, Engine plate really sets the engine off, I have a 308/Mera We'll I was just thinking of the same thing myself. Those pipes gotta go. they are peeling/rusting a little ect. I havn't really looked into what I would replace them with. Thought about powdercoating them or seeing what this chroming place here by my house could do for me. I will look into it a little more this week and post back. Thanks Larry||||reg||1
